// Style X ("Neon Pelican", docs/STYLE-X.md): the street level of a rain-slick neon megacity at night.
//   L-shore      the far side of the street: a waterfront night market on a wet deck (kiosks, market umbrellas, stools,
//                lantern strings, a watch booth, scrap, pigeons, a maintenance crab-bot, a parcel drone) in front of the
//                harbour (sea module), and the district set pieces of the route (drone dock, fish port, arcade + hologram
//                koi, the maglev viaduct and its train, the data-spire plaza, the arcology foundations, the canal, the
//                old temple).
//   L-roadside   the pavement: a lit steel barrier, cyber street lamps with overhead cables and lanterns, the maglev stop,
//                a robot cat on a bench, a parcel locker, umbrella people, the noodle stall with steam, sign pylons,
//                vending machines, holo direction boards and holo-marker kilometre stones; the neon tunnel, the
//                skybridge, the hologram statue, the pelican crossing and the WELCOME BACK banner.
//   L-road       wet asphalt: an LED kerb, grates, lane markings, glowing studs, puddles and long neon reflections.
//   L-foreground the near verge: rail, cable bundles, weeds through the cracks, litter, a glowing drain.
// Performance (STYLE-X §2): no filters at all. Neon glow is faked with stacked strokes (a wide faint halo, the tube,
// a pale core) and radial / linear gradients; every surface is static merged markup; per frame we only write
// transforms, a few display flags and low-rate opacity blinks. Sign colours are CSS custom properties with fallbacks
